What was reused:
  - The mesh files under models/xlerobot/meshes/ (except omni_wheel.stl,
    see below) come from simulation/mujoco/assets/ and simulation/xlerobot_urdf.zip
    in the upstream repository, unmodified.
  - omni_wheel.stl comes from
    simulation/mujoco/assets/simplify_4-Omni-Directional-Wheel_Single_Body-v1.stl
    in the upstream repository, unmodified.
  - The dual arm and head link and joint geometry (origins, joint limits,
    masses, inertias) in xlerobot_common.urdf.xacro was ported from the URDF
    shipped at simulation/xlerobot_urdf.zip in the upstream repository. The
    arm and head joints are currently fixed instead of actuated, this is a
    simplification made for the RoboticsAcademy integration, not part of the
    upstream model.
  - The chassis visual and collision geometry in xlerobot_common.urdf.xacro
    also comes from that same shipped URDF.

What is original to this integration, not from upstream:
  - The 3 wheel mount positions and orientations (a holonomic layout matching
    the mujoco model at simulation/mujoco/xlerobot.xml in the upstream repo,
    which is a different hardware revision than the shipped URDF above), the
    wheel collision shapes, the base_footprint frame, the xacro macro
    structure, and every Gazebo/ROS 2 plugin wiring (xlerobot_gz.urdf.xacro,
    xlerobot.launch.py).
